<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 23.23 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 23.23 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bewllether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen falling 23 basis points to 23.23 percent, and rates are also seen falling at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of 10 Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     23.46	    23.23		   - 23 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     27.73	    26.94		   - 79 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    29.91	    28.89		   -102 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     30.93	    29.75		   -118 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 (2330 GMT).</p>
<p>- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559</p>
</text>
